34,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"My findings show a lack of financial coordination. We are double-buying supplies, and the definition of ""done"" varies wildly between us.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"A full pass takes over an hour and a half. That is a significant chunk of time, especially when several tasks pile up at once.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Interestingly, the kitchen usage is heavily skewed. A few of us are creating the vast majority of the mess, yet the work is split equally.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"It's worse than we thought! Some of you think ""done"" is just wiping a counter. And the bathroom grout is a lost cause without a real plan.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I noticed in the chat that our complaints always start as ""reminders"" but quickly turn into tension. We are already fraying at the edges.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, if a full pass takes ninety minutes, the inefficiency of our current ""informal"" system is costing us more than just time.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Precisely. If we outsource, we save that time, but the firm requires us to tidy first. We aren't removing the labor entirely, just the scrubbing.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Midori, the tension in the chat is a symptom of the imbalance I found. It is logically unfair to expect a coffee-drinker to scrub a grease-caked stove.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"I don't care who makes the mess, I just care that it's clean! The unpredictability is the worst part. We need a standard that doesn't change every week.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, I understand the unfairness, but if we track every single cup of coffee, we'll end up fighting even more. We need a system that feels kind.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,We must address the money. We are wasting funds on duplicate supplies because there is no central budget or tracking.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"The professional firm is an option, but we must weigh the monthly cost against the value of our time. Is ninety minutes a week worth the fee?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"For some, yes. For those who barely use the space, paying a small fee is far more rational than performing labor for a mess they didn't create.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,I'm voting for whatever ensures the bathroom doesn't turn back into a swamp in eleven days. A professional might actually be able to handle the grout.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I'm worried that a strict ""pay-per-use"" or ""labor-per-use"" system will make us act like accountants instead of housemates. Let's keep it simple.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"Simplicity is fine, but not at the cost of transparency. Whoever pays for the bleach should be reimbursed immediately and automatically.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I am still calculating the trade-off. If we do it ourselves, we save money but lose time and risk the interpersonal friction Midori mentioned.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,The data is clear: usage and labor are currently decoupled. Any sustainable system for the next year must bridge that gap to be fair.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,Just give me a guarantee that the kitchen won't be grim on Tuesday and sparkling on Wednesday. I can't live with that rollercoaster!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"Let's look at the options. I hope we can choose the one that lets us stay friends, even if it's not the most ""efficient"" on paper.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
