60,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is the most financially transparent if we set up a shared fund. It removes the ""who did what"" argument and the ""who paid for what"" confusion.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option B removes the heavy scrubbing labor, which is the most time-consuming part. However, we still have to tidy up before they arrive.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option B is the most logical. It decouples the labor from the usage, meaning the coffee-drinkers aren't unfairly burdened by the heavy cooks' messes.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"I love Option B! A professional means a professional standard. No more guessing if the person on duty thinks ""done"" means ""I moved the dirt around.""","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I'm worried about the cost for some of us, but Option B does remove the most common source of our arguments. No one has to be the ""nag.""","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, the cost is predictable. A fixed monthly fee is better than the current chaos where some of us are out of pocket for supplies without reimbursement.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,I've compared the hours. Spending ninety minutes a week on cleaning is a significant annual loss. Paying for a service is a rational investment in our time.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,Option C is the worst choice; it simply formalizes the unfairness I discovered. It forces the low-usage residents to clean up after the high-usage ones.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"Exactly! And Option A is just a recipe for one person to let the bathroom rot for a month because they ""haven't gotten to it yet."" No thank you.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,"I agree that Option C could lead to a lot of resentment. If someone is sick or away, the rota just breaks and we start blaming each other again.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"If we go with Option B, I propose we create a dedicated supply fund. We contribute a set amount monthly to cover both the cleaner and the bleach.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,That is a sound approach. It streamlines the financial side and ensures the time-cost is minimized for everyone. I am in favor of Option B.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I concur. It is the only option that addresses the usage-labor discrepancy without requiring us to track every single dish, which would be tedious.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,I'm 100% for Option B. I want to walk into the bathroom and actually feel okay about it. Consistency is everything!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,"If everyone is this happy with Option B, then I am too. It seems like the best way to keep the peace and avoid those ""reminders"" in the chat.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Toshio,,It seems we have a consensus. Option B provides the financial clarity I require and the quality standards May wants.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,It is the most efficient use of our time. I'm satisfied with this decision.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,A rational conclusion. We trade a small amount of money for a large amount of harmony and fairness.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,Finally! I can stop bracing myself before I open the bathroom door. Let's do it!,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Midori,,I'm glad we all agree. I think this will really help us get along better over the next year. Let's vote.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
